/* Clock nudging for certificate validation.
 *
 * This board has no RTC, so at boot the clock can still read 1970, and mbedTLS
 * then rejects every server certificate on its notBefore check. Below
 * CLOCK_TLS_MIN_EPOCH we stamp a PLACEHOLDER time that sits inside the
 * validity window so the handshake can proceed. It is chosen to satisfy
 * notBefore and nothing else — it is NOT a time source, and deliberately does
 * not mark the clock verified, so callers that need a trustworthy clock
